            <ArticleTitle>Intravascular imaging and physiologic lesion assessment to define critical coronary stenoses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1547-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Despite the fact that the coronary angiogram is the gold-standard in assessing a coronary artery stenosis for the purposes of clinical decision making, it has many limitations. Alternative methods are available. This article discusses three of these: intravascular ultrasound, coronary flow reserve, and fractional flow reserve.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
